greetings everyone I'm Jeff from the  overwatch team we're here with the  developer update about overwatch year of  the rooster in particular we're really  excited to talk about the new brawl that  we added which we named capture the  rooster so as you guys know we have a  tendency to name things just a little  bit differently what you're used to  obviously capture the rooster is our  version of capture the flag and capture  the flag is a really interesting topic  for us to discuss because it's something  we've mentioned in the past as having  had a lot of trouble with when it comes  to tuning and balancing around overwatch  hero so to give you guys a little bit of  history with capture the flag we started  working on it before the game was even  announced we would do various prototypes  of different game modes and see if we  can make it work what we generally have  found with over watch over the years is  that the game works best when we have a  single objective game mode type and if  you think about control assault our  hybrids are payloads they all have one  objective you're either attacking or  defending or you need to take control of  the point or you already have that point  and you need to defend it and capture  the flag is very unique in the sense for  overwatch that there are two objectives  going on at once there's your flag the  enemy flag and you're having to decide  how many resources you dedicate to  getting their flag or to defending your  flag and both flags are on play at the  same time so we really wrestle with  capture the flag over the years for a  number of reasons the primary one is  that over watch heroes are designed  intentionally with really powerful  feeling mobility ability so obvious  examples are Ganges dash tracers blink  you've got Winston's leap Deva can fly  through the air with her boost so  there's a lot of great mobility going on  it's challenging with capture the flag  which is a very mobile game mode type  you're trying to get this thing in an  enemy base and bring it back to your own  with these types of abilities in place  so over the years as we were iterating  and testing various versions of capture  the flag we actually gave up on the mode  for a while because we felt like what we  didn't want to do was add a bunch of  rules that no longer made over watch  heroes feel like over watch heroes I'll  give you some examples of this in one of  our earliest versions that we had there  was no pickup time on the flag and we  had a character like tracer well what  our tracers would do when we were play  testing these early prototypes is they  would triple blink to the flag obviously  they would pick it up since there was no  capture time and then just hit recall  and be you know 30 meters back to where  they were literally untouchable to get  the flag and defenders of the flag  didn't even know what had happened you  know oh my god our flag is gone where  did it go well tracer is you know  already capping it so as we got into  preparing for capture the rooster and  the overwatch Lunar New Year event we  started thinking to ourselves you know  the players keep asking us for capture  the flag and there's a lot of great  suggestions in the community how to make  it work we've tried it before but should  we try it again and this time we took a  different philosophy to it so early on  when we started iteration for capture  the rooster we said well we can we can  do all these things to our heroes to try  to make it feel a lot more balanced so  we had a version up and running where we  picked the abilities that we picked were  the mobility and immunity abilities so a  great example there is Reapers Wraith  form even zenyatta ultimate  transcendence where he's moving very  fast and he also can't be damaged at all  we picked a bunch of abilities like that  tracers blink recall sombras teleport  beacon and we made it so when you use  those abilities and you were the flag  carrier you just drop the flag on the  spot and for a while we played the mode  this way thinking it would feel more  fair and somehow more about  lens and what it ended up feeling like  to us and we did a lot of play testing  on it was they just didn't feel like  overwatch characters anymore it felt  sort of like a drag almost to be the  flag carrier one of the fantasies there  was getting in grabbing that flag and  really doing the run for your base so  ironically we set up all the abilities  to drop the flag and then we ended up  reverting it all and just saying let's  really go to the spirit of what capture  the flag is to us and we believe is to  our players when we mention it to them  when people think of capture the flag  they think of those great movement  abilities in the really old school games  used to be able to grappling hook all  the way across the map with the flag and  that was one of the fun things we  remember about various CTF modes in fps  so instead of trying to overly balance  an overly tuned overwatch around this  concept of sort of fairness we said why  don't we embrace what our heroes do and  allow them to do that and really the  only couple of rules in play and our  version of capture the flag that might  be different from some of the modes that  you're used to r1 there's a little bit  of a pickup time when you get to the  flag you'll see there's a progress bar  and I'll say capturing when you're there  and it's not terribly long but any  damage interrupts that so that prevents  those really cheesy captures like tracer  triple blinking in and just pressing  recall you know now for tracer to do  that the flag has to be totally  unguarded and she needs at least enough  time to pick up the flag before she can  do that the other rule that we're trying  in capture the rooster is that we don't  require your flag to be at the base when  you capture the enemy's flag so for  those of you who are familiar with world  of warcraft we have a battleground in  there called warsong gulch and this is  something we've worked for years on and  it's one of the the favorite  battlegrounds in world of warcraft and  in world of warcraft we require you  you're too  to have the flag when when you capture  the enemy teams flag but um and it's  cool in world of warcraft because it  creates some gameplay that wasn't as fun  and over watch it was a little bit  problematic in overwatch for us when we  tried it this way where you're the flag  carrier kind of standing around trying  to communicate to your team like hey I'm  not going to be able to hold out that  much longer you guys need to go go find  the flag I can't do it on my own because  the time to kill in the lethality is a  is higher in overwatch it's more  difficult to sort of have those holdout  moments when you still have the flag now  one thing people might be worried about  is and I know we're going to hear this  feedback there are moments where you're  defending the flag your team's flag and  enemies going to come in you're going to  have a cool battle but they're going to  win and grab the flag and there's this  feeling of you know they might use some  really powerful ability Winston sleep is  a great example Winston's going to leap  away with the flagging or say well we  didn't have a chance to get that flag  and we sort of had that feeling as well  and that's why when we were in our  iteration cycle we tried those versions  where it would drop the flag when when  Winston used that leap ability what we  found during that iteration time was  usually there's a teamfight before a  flag cap happens in the first place like  an initial capture where they're  grabbing the flag from your vase and  even with the abilities dropping the  flag if the other team took the flag and  got away they were probably going to cap  it anyway whether or not we let you use  your cool movement abilities or not so  ultimately we really went with more of a  free-form capture the flag where we're  embracing more of what overwatch is  about which is your awesome hero with  your awesome abilities and letting you  use them all the time and we kind of  want to create those crazy moments where  well I didn't realize like you might  think tracer with her blink is the best  flag carrier where do you see Winston  with primal rage what he can do it's  pretty amazing  why we think this is okay is because how  we've positioned capture the rooster  with in overwatch it is in arcade mode  that's part of overwatch year the  rooster it's going to be a three week  event and the mode is going to live in  the arcade we're not adding it to quick  play the quick play rotation we're not  adding it to the competitive rotation we  don't have any plans to we just want  players to see it as a fun mode that  exists in the arcade for the sake of fun  and fun alone and we know like a mode  like mystery heroes that also exists in  the arcade it's not going to be  perfectly tuned and balance for the way  over watch works in competitive or quick  play and we're sort of okay with it  because we want it to be a blow off  steam mode that you go and do in  addition to those other modes so that's  not saying it might never be it won't  ever be a competitive mode maybe you  know some day if we fine-tune and  iterate on it it'll be great and will  think about it that way but we're not  even remotely thinking about that right  now we just want it to be fun we want it  to be for those players who have really  been vocal about asking for capture the  flag we want it to be our way of saying  we're listening to you and that you know  your feedback is important in even game  modes that we sort of had had dismissed  in the past when we hear your repeated  feedback like that we want you to know  that we care about it and we take it  really seriously so we've heard so many  requests for capture the flag we wanted  to bring it to you guys you know maybe  in the future if capture the rooster is  really successful during overwatch year  the rooster will even consider bringing  it back to the arcade in a more fully  fleshed-out version with you know new  maps and that sort of thing but  initially we want to see what your  reaction is and see how much you guys  like it will be really curious to hear  your feedback as you're playing it we  want to hear what's fun we want to hear  what you don't like about it and we'll  we'll look to that feedback to iterate  on it so in the mean  I enjoy the overwatch year the rooster  event enjoy capture the rooster as a  game-mode have lots of fun and be nice  to each other we'll see you guys  [Music]
 

